  "articleBody": "Peeling, flaking paint in a garage usually points to deeper issues than cosmetic wear. Knowing when to call a professional painter saves you time and wasted materials. Watch for these signals: - Paint is bubbling or peeling away in large sheets, indicating underlying moisture, efflorescence, or unprimed drywall. - Walls show extensive drywall gouges, settlement cracks, or water stains that need patching before repainting. - The paint was applied prior to 1978, meaning peeling layers require certified lead-safe containment and cleanup to prevent toxic dust. - Persistent exhaust fumes or chemical spills have penetrated the drywall, requiring specialty stain-blocking primers. - The project includes painting adjoining masonry, metal service doors, and textured ceilings that each require specific coatings. What Can Change the Right Choice: The condition of the underlying drywall and concrete determines whether simple scraping works or if extensive skim-coating and specialized primers are required. When you need dependable painting backed by hands-on finish carpentry and drywall experience, call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 for an estimate.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}